1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:06,060
iPhone to Windows… Android to Mac… still using a cable?

2
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:10,849
Tonight is matchday: your phone, against your computer.

3
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:17,051
The old way? Cables. The cloud. Yet another app to install.

4
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:22,060
Meet Turbodrop. Like AirDrop, for every device.

5
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:26,427
Open Turbodrop on the computer, scan the QR code with your

6
00:00:26,447 --> 00:00:30,643
phone's camera… and send. Photos, videos, folders, text.

7
00:00:30,663 --> 00:00:34,060
Nothing needs to be installed on the phone.

8
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:38,308
Wi‑Fi dropped halfway? It continues from the last chunk.

9
00:00:38,328 --> 00:00:41,191
Computers pair with a four‑emoji code.

10
00:00:41,211 --> 00:00:43,542
Nearby devices find each other.

11
00:00:43,562 --> 00:00:48,170
Photos arrive with previews, and you save them all at once as

12
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:48,625
a ZIP.

13
00:00:48,645 --> 00:00:53,253
Folders keep their structure, and duplicate files aren't sent

14
00:00:53,273 --> 00:00:58,060
again. It feels like part of Windows 11, in twelve languages.

15
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:01,181
At full Wi‑Fi speed. Connection lost?

16
00:01:01,201 --> 00:01:04,060
It continues exactly from there.

17
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:06,020
A four‑megabyte installer.

18
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:10,242
Its engine moves a gigabyte in seven and a half seconds;

19
00:01:10,262 --> 00:01:13,060
the only limit is your own network.

20
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:20,060
End‑to‑end encryption. No cloud, no account, no internet.

21
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:24,849
Windows, iPhone, Android, Mac and Linux.

22
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:29,503
For developers, there's a real command line with JSON output,

23
00:01:29,523 --> 00:01:33,582
so your AI assistant, like Claude Code, Cursor, Codex or

24
00:01:33,602 --> 00:01:38,060
Gemini CLI, can send a file to your phone with one command.

25
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:42,060
Full time! Turbodrop four, cables zero!

26
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:45,105
Turbodrop is made by Pouyam Open Source:

27
00:01:45,125 --> 00:01:49,520
free tools we build for ourselves and give to everyone, to

28
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:52,060
developers and the whole world.

29
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:55,258
It's free, it's open source. Get it from its website;

30
00:01:55,278 --> 00:01:57,398
the link is in the description.

31
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:03,217
Follow pouyamworld on Instagram and YouTube. If it helped you…

32
00:02:03,237 --> 00:02:05,566
give it a star on GitHub.
